From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:03:25 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: software_isp: Let the IPA move the focus lens

Pass the controls of the sensor's focus lens, if it has one, to the
software ISP IPA module at init time, and add a setLensControls event
that the simple pipeline handler applies to the lens, the way the IPU3
pipeline does.

Keep the lens device closed while the camera is not streaming. A lens
driver may hold the actuator, and through its device link the sensor,
powered for as long as its device node is open (dw9719 powers up on the
first focus write and down on the last close). CameraSensor opens the
lens when the camera is enumerated, and a process that keeps the camera
manager around, as the PipeWire session manager does, would otherwise
keep both powered from the first focus write on. CameraLens gains
close() and open() for this.
---
